      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-237208",
      ":question/problem": "A particular feature is being examined across $4$ groups of individuals to determine if the mean varies by group. The summary statistics of four samples, one from each group, are given in the table below, where $n_{k}$ is the size of each sample, and $x^(\u2015)_{k}$ is the sample mean.\n\n|  | Sample 1 | Sample 2 | Sample 3 | Sample 4 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $n_{k}$ | $10$ | $8$ | $12$ | $10$ |\n| $x_{k}^(\u2015)$ | $1.5$ | $1.8$ | $1.8$ | $1.7$ |\n\nWhat is the sum of squares between groups (SSB) of these samples?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
