      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-252250",
      ":question/problem": "A particular feature is being examined across $3$ groups of individuals to determine if the mean varies by group. The summary statistics of three samples, one from each group, are given in the table below, where $n_{k}$ is the size of each sample, and $x^(\u2015)_{k}$ is the sample mean.\n\n|  | Sample 1 | Sample 2 | Sample 3 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $n_{k}$ | $19$ | $29$ | $20$ |\n| $x_{k}^(\u2015)$ | $4.4$ | $3.6$ | $4.2$ |\n\nWhat is the sum of squares between groups (SSB) of these samples?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
